A module whose production code imports a path below node_modules that names a
regular file rather than a directory. The path holds no package, so it derives
no configuration, and the load reports the import.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27.0
-- main.go --
package main

import "example.com/app/node_modules/helper"

func main() { helper.Run() }
-- node_modules/helper --
not a directory
